      "id": 1,
      "text": "Hollowville was once called Smoky Hollow, a name that hints at its early days when smoke from local mills filled the valley.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://townofclaverack.com/town-life/villages-hamlets/hollowville/"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The hamlet grew along the Columbia Turnpike, now County Route 23, where water power from Claverack Creek once ran early mills.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://townofclaverack.com/town-life/villages-hamlets/hollowville/"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A tavern built in the 1800s on a hill still stands today and continues to serve patrons, a living link to Hollowville’s past.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://usgennet.org/usa/ny/county/columbia/clav/holo.htm"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Peter I operates a cradle‑factory in Hollowville, a niche manufacturing spot that keeps the hamlet’s industrial heritage alive.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
